From 60c18a241e50ae89b2b616914cd21690d47ac8b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: claim deferrals carry their origin; skip
 words read it, not a name list

PR #2003 (review 5888302963, nit) worded a claim_deferred skip as "this host's admission gate" from a
name-prefix list (hub_cpu_*, hub_admission_overrun, hub_capacity_full). This host's other refusals
(update_admission_hold, the disk admission refusals, worker_resources_unknown, the worker-resource
refusal() codes, the placement/worker-capacity refusals in claim_gate) still read "the Board deferred
its claim", and a Board lease reason spelt like a local one would read as local.

kanban_db_sync.ClaimDeferral is a str carrying origin ("local" | "board"), stamped where the deferral is
produced: kanban_admission._defer and claim_gate's execution_refusal / waiting_for_worker_capacity are
local; the Board lease refusal and the unreachable service ("offline") are board. Every consumer that
compares or prints the reason is unchanged. The dispatch skip records origin in its payload (and the
notice fields), and words() picks the wording from it. A skip without an origin keeps the Board default.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_claim_deferral_origin.py (RED on base: update hold, disk refusal and
worker_resources_unknown worded as Board; a Board "hub_capacity_full" refusal worded as local).
